From: GT-I9082L Pie Go Project <i9082l-pie-go@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] binder: prevent -ERESTARTSYS (-512) from leaking to userspace on suspend/wake

On Linux 3.0.101 ARM32, PM freezer / suspend wakeups can interrupt
binder_thread_read() and cause binder_ioctl() to return -ERESTARTSYS (-512)
without a pending userspace signal. Android 9 IPCThreadState aborts
SurfaceFlinger on unexpected errno -512, leaving the screen black after
suspend/wake. Convert -ERESTARTSYS without signal_pending(current) to
-EINTR, which IPCThreadState retries cleanly.

---
diff --git a/drivers/staging/android/binder.c b/drivers/staging/android/binder.c
index 92305f7..20f58c3 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/android/binder.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/android/binder.c
@@ -3368,6 +3368,8 @@ err:
 	if (ret && ret != -ERESTARTSYS)
 		pr_info("%d:%d ioctl %x %lx returned %d\n", proc->pid, current->pid, cmd, arg, ret);
 err_unlocked:
+	if (ret == -ERESTARTSYS && !signal_pending(current))
+		ret = -EINTR;
 	trace_binder_ioctl_done(ret);
 	return ret;
 }
